From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0816: the reload skip stays while elided stores live (the MISS after a live flip); resolve_elide_keep_file keeps learned readers across runs (Direct3D 12; native stream, zero-copy session 3)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; scratch/zerocopy3/TESTPLAN3.md). Written without a build or a run: checked with
  clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of d3d12/resolve_elide.cpp, d3d12/texture_cache.cpp,
  d3d12/command_processor.cpp and units that include d3d12/texture_cache.h; 0 errors, no warning on an added line. Needs 0815.
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: 1. Session 2's MISS after a live flip (s2-cyc1: `[resolve-elide] mode 0 (off), was 2` and the MISS in the same
  millisecond): switching resolve_elide and resolve_reinterpret_reload off together left the stores elided under the reload skip
  live, and the next load of the 8888 texture at 0x06CEE000 (outdated only by other surfaces' resolves) was made again, over the
  elided depth store. While any elided record is live the reload skip now stays (as 1) until stores made after the switch
  overwrite them. 2. New cvar resolve_elide_keep_file (bool, default true, at start; only with resolve_elide on and a draw scale
  above 1): <cache>/shaders/shareable/<title>.resolve-keep.txt holds one rule a line of the destinations a load of their own
  layout read; they are kept (stored) from the start of the next runs; a newly read one is appended. Opened where the render target
  cache opens its key file (D3D12CommandProcessor::InitializeShaderStorage). `[resolve-elide] keep file: N destinations ...` at
  start; a MISS says whether its rule came from the file. (A record kind of the .xrtp key file was not used: its records are one
  32-bit key, a rule is six.)
Bucket: REDO

0816-elide-flip-keep-file.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy session 3).

